Greenplum Database Upgrader
---------------------------

This directory contains code for upgrade a 3.0 series Greenplum Database
to 3.1. Do not use this for anything but migrating between 3.0 and 3.1.

This code is !!ALPHA!!

1) Directory contents

gpupgrade
---------

This binary is the tool which does the actual upgrading. It's architecture
is described here:

http://intranet.greenplum.com:8080/confluence/download/attachments/4981/upgrade.pdf?version=2

The actual details might have diverged a little but the approach is the same.

For usage, --help has everything you want.

gp_controldata_mod
------------------

This binary switches a pg_control data file from the 3.0 to the 3.1 catalog
versions (and vice versa). It is used by gpstart and shouldn't be used
directly unless a problem is encountered, etc.

gpupgradefuncs.so
-----------------

This library provides backend functions used by the upgrade process.

gendbkidiff.pl
--------------

A tool to generate SQL based on the difference between different BKI files,
representing different catalog versions. It's still alpha and spits lots of
debugging output at you but it can generate a C header file suited for
upgrading a cluster.

2) Current status

a) Downgrading from 3.1 to 3.0 doesn't work. This still needs intensive work.

<DONE>
b) Serialised parser nodes are not rewritten to the 3.1 parse node format
at the moment. This means views and rules from 3.0, when we upgrade to 3.1,
will probably not work. You'll see errors like:

ERROR:  unrecognized token: "RTE"

if you access a view by mistake.
</DONE>

c) General polishing, comments, doc/help updates need doing

The first two are absolute necessities for alpha1.

3) Performing and upgrade/downgrade

WARNING: This tool is not suitable for production data yet. It is in
testing for alpha1.

1) gpstop                                                                       
2) install new binaries                                                         
3) <3.1>gpstart -u 3.1 # <3.1> means the 3.1 version must be used               
4) <3.1>gpupgrade                                                               
5) <3.1>gpstop                                                                  
6) <3.1>gpstart # no upgrade options                                            
                                                                                
The upgrade option to gpstart is only recognised as of 3.1. The 3.1             
gpstart does some configuration changes to support running an upgrade --        
such as allowing system catalog modifications. It also changes                  
pg_control.                                                                     
                                                                                
Downgrading looks like this:                                                    
                                                                                
1) <3.1>gpstop                                                                  
2) <3.1>gpstart -u 3.0 # notice that we're downgrading to 3.0!                  
3) <3.1>gpupgrade -D # -D for downgrade                                         
4) <3.1>gpstop                                                                  
5) <3.0>gpstart

4) Standby Master and the upgrader

The architecture of the QD standby makes it difficult to upgrade QD standbys.
Since, the removal and initialisation of QD standbys is trivial, an extra
step is required if you are upgrading such a system: before any of the
steps listed above, remove the standby segment from the cluster; after the
upgrade is complete, add it back again with ``gpinitstandby''. This is the
case for both upgrades and downgrades.

Gavin <gavin@alcove.com.au>
